###############################################################################
#  Byte-verbatim vendor disk images and their catalog listings. Nothing here
#  may be transformed on checkout.
#
#  The disks are obvious enough. The catalog listings are the trap: they are
#  plain LF-only text, so under the root's `* text=auto` and core.autocrlf
#  git would hand a Windows clone CRLF copies. The bytes would then no longer
#  match the SHA-256 values pinned in README.md and in scripts/FetchMerlin.ps1,
#  and the provenance chain back to archive.org -- the entire reason to trust
#  these files -- would report a mismatch on a clean checkout with nothing
#  actually wrong.
#
#  So the listings are pinned alongside the images rather than treated as the
#  ordinary text they otherwise resemble.
###############################################################################
* binary

# The documentation is ordinary text and should behave that way. `binary` is a
# macro for `-diff -merge -text`, so restoring diff and merge takes saying so.
README.md      text=auto diff merge
.gitattributes text=auto diff merge
